            "commentId": "peer-over-cap",
            "commentUid": "student-7",
            "content": "You explained who the design is for, but the explanation runs on and repeats itself. Start by naming the person who uses this, then say what problem they have, then say how your design solves that problem. At the moment those three things are mixed together in one long paragraph, so a reader has to work out which sentence is doing which job. Try splitting it into three short paragraphs and cutting anything that says the same thing twice. It would also help to say how old the user is and where they would be standing when they use it, because that changes what the buttons need to look like.",
